# Native AI SDK DevTools Integration

## Context & Goals

Mux currently has a stub integration with `@ai-sdk/devtools` gated behind `MUX_DEVTOOLS=1` env var
(in `providerModelFactory.ts` line 519). It requires spawning a separate Hono HTTP viewer on port
4983. We want to replace this with a **first-party, in-process implementation** that:

1. Records all AI SDK `generateText`/`streamText` calls (runs & steps) per-workspace
2. Stores debug logs in `~/.mux/sessions/{workspaceId}/devtools.jsonl`
3. Streams events to the frontend over existing oRPC (no HTTP server, no extra process)
4. Renders a native **Debug** tab in the right sidebar
5. Is gated by an **"LLM Debug Logs"** toggle in Settings (persisted in `config.json`)

### Acceptance Criteria

The feature is **done** when:
- [ ] Toggling "LLM Debug Logs" ON in Settings causes all subsequent `streamText`/`generateText` calls to record runs/steps
- [ ] Toggling it OFF stops recording (no data written, middleware is no-op)
- [ ] The Debug tab in the right sidebar shows a live-updating list of runs for the current workspace
- [ ] Clicking a run shows its steps with input/output/usage/timing/error detail
- [ ] Data persists across app restart (loaded from `devtools.jsonl`)
- [ ] Corrupted JSONL lines are skipped on load (self-healing, never crashes)
- [ ] `@ai-sdk/devtools` npm dependency is removed
- [ ] All tests pass: `make test`, `make typecheck`, `make lint`

### Reference Code

The upstream source at `./tmpfork/vercel/ai/packages/devtools/` is useful for:
- `src/middleware.ts` lines 200–390: `TransformStream` interception pattern for `wrapStream`
- `src/db.ts` lines 36–58: Data model (`Run`, `Step`, `StepResult` interfaces)
- `src/viewer/client/app.tsx`: UI patterns (run list, step cards, input/output tabs)

